## PERCEPTION

Enemy detection must account for:

* Field of view.
* Distance.
* Line of sight.
* Lighting where implemented.
* Player movement.
* Noise.
* Nearby allied alerts.
* Time since last detection.

Enemies must not see through solid walls.

When line of sight is lost, enemies should search the last known position rather than automatically knowing the player's new position.

## COVER AND TACTICS

Implement tactical cover selection.

Enemies should:

* Evaluate available cover.
* Avoid exposed positions when appropriate.
* Change positions when a cover location becomes unsafe.
* Avoid all choosing the same position.
* Use flanking routes where available.
* Coordinate attacks when the game rules permit.
* Stop pursuing when their behavior or mission rules require them to return to a defensive area.

## PERSONALITIES

Retain the existing enemy classes:

* Guard.
* Assault.
* Defender.
* Scout.
* Elite.

Give each class meaningful behavioral differences.

Do not make elite enemies unfair by allowing them to track the player through walls or apply unexplained damage bonuses.

## PERFORMANCE

Do not run expensive pathfinding for every enemy on every rendered frame.

Use controlled AI update intervals and navigation caching where appropriate.

Ensure enemies can recover from failed routes.

Test navigation around obstacles and diagonal corners.

